hh;106909769;not_active;07.09.2024;12.09.2024;Москва;9201947;;;;Senior DevSecOps Engineer;DevOps-инженер;;4000;6000;EUR;ЛОЖЬ;Нет опыта;Полный день;Полная занятость;;"SHORT DESCRIPTION This position requires on-site work from one of our offices in Riga, Budva or Barcelona. We are looking for a highly skilled and driven individual to join our team as a DevSecOps Engineer. In this role, you will be responsible for designing, developing, and implementing the DevSecOps framework for our industry-leading B2B betting platform, leveraging cutting-edge and the most efficient security technologies. MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS Minimum of 3 years of experience in a similar role, with a proven track record. Willingness and ability to work on-site at our offices in Riga, Budva or Barcelona. REQUIREMENTS Strong expertise in the Secure Development Lifecycle (SDLC) and web application security. In-depth understanding of modern threats and advanced threat modelling techniques. Extensive hands-on experience with integrating at least three different security tools within CI/CD pipelines. Hands-on experience in creating automation tools using any programming language, such as Python, Java, Bash or PowerShell. Proficiency in securing cloud-native applications using well-established methodologies. Comprehensive knowledge of Kubernetes security practices and mitigation strategies. Proficiency in English at an intermediate level or higher. WOULD BE AN ADVANTAGE Professional certifications in Information Security, such as CKA, CKS, CDP, or equivalents. Practical experience in secure coding or close collaboration with security champions. Familiarity with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) security tools and practices. RESPONSIBILITIES Define and continuously refine security solutions and best practices within the continuous integration and delivery (CI/CD) pipeline. Perform service-level threat modelling to anticipate and mitigate potential security risks. Ensure the security of DevOps tools and processes, including Source Control, Containerization, Continuous Integration, and Change Management. Manage, prioritise and partially implement the backlog of CI/CD pipeline hardening tasks and security checks integration in close collaboration with Infrastructure and DevOps teams. Identify, assess, and prioritise vulnerabilities in the product, development processes and tools used throughout the CI/CD lifecycle including performing security assessments and using automated scanning tools to detect weaknesses. Developing, managing and implementing remediation plans to fix identified vulnerabilities, ensuring they are resolved promptly. Implement robust access control mechanisms to regulate access to critical information resources. Conduct regular security audits and enhance practices related to secret management, vulnerability management, network segmentation, system hardening, integrity control, incident monitoring, and response in cloud and containerized environments. Provide security training to team members, raising awareness of potential threats and promoting secure architecture and coding practices. Evaluate emerging technologies and security tools to select the most effective solutions for our environment. PERKS AND BENEFITS Join our dynamic product company and experience a recruiting process like no other one that is both timesaving and highly efficient. Why choose us? Heres what we offer: Comprehensive health insurance to ensure your well-being. Enjoy the peace of mind with 100% paid sick leaves. Fuel your professional growth with access to extra education opportunities. Recharge and relax with a generous 20 working days of paid vacation and additional days off. We've got your back if youre ready to relocate receive full support throughout the process. Be part of a vibrant international team united by a shared passion for excellence in product development. Enhance your language skills with language courses tailored to your needs. Unleash your inner adventurer with